        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Moorcock, Colonel Pyat, Ernst Julius Günther Röhm\n- Works: The Vengeance of Rome\n- Places: Italy, Dachau\n- Concepts: Eternal Champion, Fascism, Nazism\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Moorcock published The Vengeance of Rome in 2006.\n- The Vengeance of Rome is a novel featuring Colonel Pyat.\n- Colonel Pyat is described as an incarnation of the Eternal Champion.\n- In The Vengeance of Rome, Colonel Pyat goes to Italy and Dachau.\n- In The Vengeance of Rome, Colonel Pyat becomes involved in Fascism and Nazism.\n- In The Vengeance of Rome, Colonel Pyat has sexual encounters with Ernst Julius Günther Röhm.\n- Ernst Julius Günther Röhm is described as a Dachau military officer and an early member of the Nazi Party.",
