        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Colonel Pyat, Ernst Röhm, Adolf Hitler\n- Works: The Vengeance of Rome\n- Places: Italy, Germany, Dachau\n- Organizations: Nazi Party\n- Concepts: Fascism, Nazism\n- Roles: German military officer\n\nFacts:\n- Ernst Röhm was born on 28 November 1887.\n- Ernst Röhm was a German military officer and an early member of the Nazi Party.\n- In The Vengeance of Rome, Colonel Pyat is described as an incarnation of the Eternal Champion.\n- In The Vengeance of Rome, Colonel Pyat goes to Italy and Germany and becomes involved in Fascism and Nazism.\n- In The Vengeance of Rome, Colonel Pyat has sexual encounters with Ernst Röhm and Adolf Hitler and spends time in Dachau.\n- Ernst Röhm died on 1 July 1934.",
